# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
god_exists	one
essence_involves_existence	one
# P2 reads S5's "this is absurd" (citing Prop. vii) as asserting that God's essence involves existence. P1 denies that same claim. One statement asserts it and the other denies it, so the sense stays the same.
# "exists" means actual existence both in P1, under "possibly not", and in C, under "necessarily". The modal operators sit outside the claim and do not change what "exists" means.
